          <Button variant="secondary" href="/studio">See the studio</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==========================================================
         Studio + app
    ========================================================== -->
    <section class="sheet sheet--navy section" id="studio-app" data-spot>
      <div class="grain sheet__grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="container sa">
        <div class="sa__text">
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--orange" data-reveal>Studio + app</span>
          <h2 class="headline h2 sa__title" data-reveal>
            Our studio makes it in the app, and you <span class="accent">approve</span> it there.
          </h2>
          <p class="sa__body" data-reveal>
            With Studio + app, our creatives make the work inside hubStudio. Your people get
            client logins and a Client space that shows only what was made for them. They
            download it, comment on it, and approve it or send it back in Validation. They never
            see prompts, engines or costs.
          </p>
          <p class="sa__body" data-reveal>
            If your team already uses hubStudio, we can work in your workspace instead. You add
            our creatives as members, we create from your balance, and your admins approve. The
            files stay in your History and Assets Library when the project ends. In both setups
            the versions stay on one approval thread, and nothing on it can be deleted.
          </p>
          <a class="arrow-link arrow-link--light" href="/studio/with-the-app" data-reveal>
            How Studio + app works <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="sa__visual" data-reveal>
          <div class="sa__photo">
            <img
              src="/Images/studio-on-app.webp"
              alt="A hubStudio producer talks through a shot list on a video call at a desk by a window, a laptop open beside him."
