          Building your own AI content team? See <a href="/solutions/consulting">consulting</a>
          and <a href="/solutions/training">training</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==========================================================
         How paying works (no amounts)
    ========================================================== -->
    <section class="sheet sheet--light section" id="pricing">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="s-head">
          <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Pricing</span>
          <h2 class="headline h2" data-reveal>
            Two offers, two ways to <span class="accent">pay</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="pay__updated" data-reveal>
            Updated <time datetime="2026-09">September 2026</time>
          </p>
          <p class="s-head__intro" data-reveal>
            The app runs on a prepaid balance you top up, while the studio quotes each job once
            it has read your brief. We don’t publish rates here, but you never have to guess: in
            the app, each engine’s card in Explore shows what one run costs, and the price shows
            again before you run it. Creating an account costs nothing, so you can see every
            price before you top up.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="pay">
          <article class="pay__card pay__card--app" data-reveal style="--i:0">
            <h3 class="pay__title">The app: a prepaid balance</h3>
            <p class="pay__text">
              You top up by card, Alipay or WeChat Pay and get an invoice each time. Every run is
              charged against that balance at the price you saw before running it, and a failed
              run is never charged.
            </p>
            <p class="pay__text">
              There’s no subscription and no seat fee, and the balance doesn’t expire. The whole
              team draws on one balance, and an admin can set a daily limit per person. The Image
              editor, the Image anonymizer, the Video editor and Validation cost nothing to use.
            </p>
            <div class="pay__cta">
              <Button variant="primary" href={APP_SIGNUP}>Create your account</Button>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="pay__card pay__card--studio" data-reveal style="--i:1">
            <h3 class="pay__title">The studio: per asset, per project or on retainer</h3>
            <p class="pay__text">
              Send a brief and a producer reads it within one business day. A written proposal
              follows within 48 hours, with the scope and the price.
            </p>
            <p class="pay__text">
              Volume formats are usually priced per asset, launches per project. A retainer suits
              teams that need new work every week.
            </p>
            <div class="pay__cta">
              <Button variant="secondary" href={BRIEF_URL}>Send a brief</Button>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="block-more" data-reveal>
          <a class="arrow-link pay__more" href="/pricing">
            See how pricing works <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==========================================================
         What we believe
    ========================================================== -->
    <section class="sheet sheet--ink believe">
      <div class="grain sheet__grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
